Okay, then I think you can hack this bit of `src/cpu/dynarmic_wrapper/build.rs`:

```
    link_lib(if cfg!(debug_assertions) {
        "fmtd"
    } else {
        "fmt"
    });
```

> when compiling it this way, you need to explicitly link to macOS frameworks

Ah, yeah, I think I remember having this issue when I tried to dynamically link SDL2. Sorry for forgetting about it.

> Now, the undefined symbol [is part of dynarmic](https://github.com/merryhime/dynarmic/tree/master/externals/zydis) […] `_Zydis` […]

Probably the fault of this code in `src/cpu/dynarmic_wrapper/build.rs`:

```rust
    #[cfg(target_arch = "x86_64")]
    {
        link_search(
            &dynarmic_out
                .join("build/externals/zydis")
                .join(build_type_windows()),
        );
        link_lib("Zydis");
    }
```
